---
title: "What is Lesli? — Build SaaS and Business Software with Rails"
description: "Lesli is an open-source Rails framework that provides a modular foundation and reusable capabilities for building SaaS and business software."
---

<header class="about-header">
    <%= partial("partials/lesli-navigation", locals: { logo: true }) %>

    <div class="container about-hero">
        <p class="about-eyebrow">Lesli in one minute</p>
        <h1>Build SaaS and business software <span class="lesli-title-colored">without rebuilding the foundation.</span></h1>
        <p class="about-introduction">
            Lesli is an open-source framework that adds a modular foundation to a Ruby on Rails application.
            Your team gets reusable building blocks while owning the code, data, and product.
        </p>

        <ul class="about-pillars" aria-label="What Lesli provides">
            <li class="about-pillar about-pillar--product">
                <span class="about-pillar-icon ri-code-s-slash-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <strong>Build real products</strong>
                <span>Create SaaS platforms, internal tools, customer portals, and workflow systems.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="about-pillar about-pillar--capabilities">
                <span class="about-pillar-icon ri-stack-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <strong>Reuse the essentials</strong>
                <span>Add modules for access control, auditing, notifications, administration, and more.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="about-pillar about-pillar--ownership">
                <span class="about-pillar-icon ri-box-3-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <strong>Own the result</strong>
                <span>Choose what you need and keep your workflows, integrations, brand, and data.</span>
            </li>
        </ul>

    </div>
</header>

<main class="about-content">
    <section class="about-explanation">
        <div class="container">
            <p class="about-section-label">How Lesli helps</p>
            <h2>A shared foundation. A product that stays yours.</h2>
            <p class="about-explanation-copy">
                Start with a normal Rails application. Lesli Core provides the shared structure. Ready-made modules
                add common capabilities; custom modules contain the workflows unique to your product. Lesli handles
                the repeatable foundation so your team can focus on how the business works.
            </p>

            <figure class="about-diagram">
                <img
                    src="/images/engines/lesli/structure.excalidraw.svg"
                    alt="Three-step diagram showing a Rails application using Lesli Core and optional modules to become an owned SaaS product"
                    loading="lazy"
                />
            </figure>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-use">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="about-use-copy">
                <p class="about-section-label">For developers</p>
                <h2>From Rails app to Lesli in three commands.</h2>
                <p>
                    Install the core, prepare its database, and then add only the official or custom modules your
                    product needs.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="about-code" aria-label="Lesli quick start commands">
                <div class="about-code-heading">
                    <span>Quick start</span>
                    <span>Terminal</span>
                </div>
                <pre><code>bundle add lesli
bin/rails generate lesli:install
bin/rails lesli:db:prepare</code></pre>
                <a href="/engines/lesli/start/">
                    Read the full installation guide
                    <span class="ri-arrow-right-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
